          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The hex color value is likely most familiar to web developers. The value must be either 3 or 6 characters (case insensitive) with an optional leading hash ("
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "#"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "), optional surrounding quotes, or both."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "To align with CSS, you may add a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "#"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in front of the hex color value. A YAML preprocessor is used to ensure the value is not treated as a comment as would normally be the case in YAML. That same preprocessor will also coerce a primitive value to a string if "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "color"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is the name of the last segment in the key (e.g., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "font-color"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). This avoids the problem of 000 becoming 0 (and similar implicit conversions) when the theme file is parsed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You also may put quotes around the CSS-style hex value to make it friendly to a YAML editor or validation tool. In this case, the leading "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "#"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " on a hex value is entirely optional."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Regardless, we recommend that you always use either a leading "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "#"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or surrounding quotes (or both) to prevent YAML from mangling the value."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The following are all equivalent values for the color red:"
