      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "A CMYK array value must be four numbers ranging from 0 and 1 or from 0% to 100%. The values must be separated by commas and be surrounded by square brackets."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Unlike the RGB array, the CMYK array "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "is not"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "emphasis",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " converted to a hex string internally. PDF has native support for CMYK colors, so you can preserve the original color values in the final PDF."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Here’s how to specify the color red in CMYK:"
